{"id": "EUVD-2026-102486", "enisaUuid": "27b02ed6-eaff-3a1e-848d-28e6fda82677", "description": "OxiCloud 0.9.1 through 0.9.3 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability that allows anonymous visitors to keep share access after password protection is added. Attackers holding an existing oxi_shares share-ring cookie can request content via GET /api/files/{id} to read shared files or folder contents despite the new password.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T21:43:35", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/oxicloud-share-password-grant-not-revoked", "https://github.com/AtalayaLabs/OxiCloud/blob/v0.9.3/src/application/services/share_service.rs#L497-L538", "https://github.com/AtalayaLabs/OxiCloud/blob/v0.9.3/src/infrastructure/services/share_ring.rs#L173-L195", "https://github.com/AtalayaLabs/OxiCloud", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/oxicloud-0.9.1-through-0.9.3-incorrect-authorization-via-share-ring-cookie"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111332", "GHSA-j8xc-5qc2-7pc3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e194fe4a-2198-3919-9625-cdb7d7aee086", "product": {"name": "OxiCloud", "vendor": {"name": "AtalayaLabs"}}, "product_version": "0.9.1 \u22640.9.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2d049673-79c9-30c7-9171-eba64744ea63", "vendor": {"name": "AtalayaLabs"}}], "isExploited": false}